:\nATTORNEY FOR (name):  | FOR COURT USE ONLY\n--- | ---\nPLAINTIFF/PETITIONER:\nDEFENDANT/RESPONDENT:\nOTHER:  | \nORDER TO FILE\nNEW LITIGATION BY VEXATIOUS LITIGANT\nType of case: Limited Civil Unlimited Civil Small Claims\nFamily Law Probate Other  | \n | CASE NUMBER:ORDER\nApproval to file the attached document is:\nGranted\na.\nDenied\nb.\nOther:\nc.\nAttachment to order.\nNumber of pages:\nDate:\nPRESIDING JUDGE OR JUSTICE\nPage 1 of 1\nCode of Civil Procedure, § 391.7 \nwww.courts.ca.gov\nForm Approved for Optional Use \nJudicial Council of California \nVL-115 [Rev. September 1, 2018]\nORDER TO FILE \nNEW LITIGATION BY VEXATIOUS LITIGANT\nPrint this form\nSave this form\nClear this form\nFor your protection and privacy, please press the Clear \nThis Form button after you have printed the form.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOrder to File New Litigation by Vexatious Litigant | California Courts | Self Help Guide (https://www.selfhelp.courts.ca.gov/jcc-form/VL-115)\nciteturn1722search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; # Order to File New Litigation by Vexatious Litigant (VL-115)States the court’s decision (order) whether a person who is subject to a prefiling vexatious litigant order can or cannot file a document in a California court.\n\n# Order to File New Litigation by Vexatious Litigant (VL-115)\n\nStates the court’s decision (order) whether a person who is subject to a prefiling vexatious litigant order can or cannot file a document in a California court.\n\nGet form VL-115\n\nEffective: September 1, 2018--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nVexatious Litigant List | Judicial Branch of California (https://courts.ca.gov/news-reference/reports-publications/vexatious-litigant-list)\nciteturn1722search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; This optional form may be used by an individual that has been determined to be a vexatious litigant and who must obtain prior court approval to file any new litigation in which the vexatious litigant is not represented by an attorney. ... VL-115, Order to File New Litigation by a Vexatious Litigant ... If you have any questions about this list, please contact VexatiousLitigantGroup@jud.ca.gov.\nFiling new litigation means (1) commencing any civil action or proceeding, or (2) filing any petition, application, or motion (except a discovery motion) under the Family or Probate Code in the courts of California.\n\nVL-115, Order to File New Litigation by a Vexatious Litigant\nThis new optional form is the order portion of Request to File New Litigation by Vexatious Litigant (form VL-110).\n\nVL-120, Application for Order to Vacate Prefiling Order and Remove Plaintiff/Petitioner from Judicial Council Vexatious Litigant List\nThis new optional form may be used by a vexatious litigant to ask to be removed from the list of vexatious litigants who must obtain prefiling approval.\n\nVL-125, Order on Application to Vacate Prefiling Order and Remove Plaintiff/Petitioner from Judicial Council Vexatious Litigant List\nThis new optional form is an order to be used to grant or deny the vexatious litigant’s request to be removed from the list.\n\nContact\n\nIf you have any questions about this list, please contact VexatiousLitigantGroup@jud.ca.gov.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n| California Courts | Self Help Guide (https://selfhelp.courts.ca.gov/find-forms/all-by-category)\nciteturn1722search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 5 days ago;   * CH-115 * Request to Continue Court Hearing (Temporary Restraining Order) Effective: January 1, 2020 汉语 한국어 español Tiếng Việt ...   * UD-116 Declaration for Default Judgment by Court (Unlawful Detainer—Civ. ...   * VL-115 Order to File New Litigation by Vexatious Litigant Effective: September 1, 2018\n\nSee form info Download\n\n  * VL-110 Request to File New Litigation by Vexatious Litigant Effective: September 1, 2018\n\nSee